{
  "about": "The encoding coverage list of the A64 decoder (docs/arm64-virt-android16-plan.md P2.1): every class of the Arm ARM's encoding index (DDI 0487 L.b, C4.1) with its status in profile v86-aarch64-v1 (implemented; undef: unallocated or a feature v1 does not declare; hint: executes as NOP; id-space: reads as zero at EL1), the feature, what the class raises, and the tests that cover it. tests/a64/decode_check.mjs holds the decoder to llvm-mc over every listed class (all fields of the small classes, the FP/SIMD group exhaustively but for registers, a stratified sample of the rest); the oracles hold the execution to QEMU and, for FP/SIMD/crypto, to an Apple M1 Pro.",
  "profile": "v86-aarch64-v1",
  "statuses": {
    "implemented": "decoded and executed",
    "undef": "UNDEFINED (EC 0x00): unallocated, or a feature profile v1 does not declare",
    "hint": "a HINT the profile does not implement: executes as NOP",
    "id-space": "an unallocated ID register: reads 0 at EL1, UNDEF at EL0"
  },
  "classes": [
    { "group": "Reserved", "class": "UDF and the rest of op0 = 0000", "status": "undef", "tests": ["decode_check"] },
    { "group": "SME, SVE", "class": "op0 = 1xxx 000x, 0010", "status": "undef", "feature": "FEAT_SME, FEAT_SVE", "tests": ["decode_check"] },

    { "group": "Data Processing -- Immediate", "class": "PC-rel. addressing", "status": "implemented", "instructions": ["adr", "adrp"], "tests": ["decode_check", "integer_oracle"] },
